# .linkmap — where caelestia-dots/caelestia's directories belong under $HOME.
#
# Read by ./link.sh rice caelestia. It lives here rather than at the root of
# that checkout because the checkout is upstream's: a file added there is
# untracked noise in its `git status` and is gone the next time it is cloned.
#
# Format: <path in the caelestia repo>  <path under $HOME>. Blank lines and #
# ignored. Only files are linked, directory by directory, so anything you drop
# into the target that is not upstream's survives — which is what makes
# ~/.config/hypr/scheme/current.lua, written by the config itself on first
# load, harmless.

hypr     .config/hypr

# Deliberately not linked:
#
#   the shell           not in this repo at all. On Arch it is the
#                       caelestia-shell AUR package: a quickshell config built
#                       against a C++ plugin and installed system wide, so
#                       there is nothing here to point at. RICE_PKGS in link.sh
#                       is what checks for it.
#
#   fish, foot, btop,   this repo's own packages own those paths and they are
#   fastfetch, micro,   rice neutral — the desktop changing is no reason for
#   starship, thunar    the shell prompt and the terminal to change with it.
#                       Same call the imperative-dots map made about kitty.
#                       caelestia-cli still colours btop and cava from the
#                       current scheme; it writes a caelestia.theme of its own
#                       next to the rainynight one and does not touch it.
#
#   vscode, zed         the editor is not part of the desktop.
#
#   firefox, spicetify  they install into a browser profile and a spotify
#                       install, not into ~/.config, and copying them is
#                       nothing a symlinker can undo.
#
#   uwsm                this machine starts Hyprland from start-hyprland, not
#                       through uwsm, so its env files would never be read.
#
#   packages, manifest  upstream's own installer and PKGBUILDs. `caelestia
#   .toml               install` is precisely the thing not to run here: it
#                       copies these dots over ~/.config with no way back.
